it might not look like it but these  people are providing a vital service  [Music]  without any external funding anya and  her friends deliver groceries and basic  goods to some of the most vulnerable in  kiev  some of the goods are donated but most  are paid for by the volunteers  themselves  i always wanted to do humanitarian work  i don't have grandparents so this helps  me compensate for that it really comes  from my heart  maria rarely leaves the house she's too  frail to make the journey and the  elevator in her building is best  described as temperamental  she stayed in the city because she says  she has no family to go to without the  volunteers she'll be completely alone  and hungry  i was in hospital with heart problems  and my daughter died recently  i have a niece who could help but public  transport is shut so she can't get here  right now i don't need anything because  they brought me things but this won't  last long  the volunteers work under the umbrella  of an organization called love life  which existed before the war to help the  homeless and vulnerable  now it's one of the only organizations  of its kind in ukraine still operating  and demand for its services far  outstrips its capacity  to cope the organization has changed the  way it operates it identifies the most  vulnerable people and posts them on a  private social media channel  volunteers then make the deliveries  navigating the city's many checkpoints  and anti-tank barricades  and it's not just home delivery  kitchens and roadside kiosks have also  become a front line of sorts in the war  effort  most of the restaurants across the city  are shut but the kitchens are open and  the chefs are working now they might not  be making their usual cuisines what  they're doing is they're making  home-style cuisines that then volunteers  pick up and bring to distribution points  like these and it is a lifeline for many  this might be the one hot meal that they  get a day imran khan al jazeera kiev
 

